WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.133
-Reese.
-Yes.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.901
-You know we love you.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:06.634
Thanks for being here. I want
to talk about "Busy Betty."

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.234
-Oh, yes!
-I also want to talk about --

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.834
You're in New York.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.234
You're doing "The Morning Show"
here in New York.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.968
-Yeah, we're shooting
"The Morning Show" in New York.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.534
-So, I love -- I love that show.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.567
I think we talked about it
last time you were on here.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.567
But we had Jon Hamm on recently,

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.200
and he said that
he's joining the cast.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.834
-The Hamm. Yes!
-Jon Hamm is joining the cast?

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:30.267
-I know.
And we are beyond excited.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.934
-He's the greatest.
-He's the greatest.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.334
-Can you -- What can you say --

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.033
Or you can't say
what his character is?

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.267
-Not allowed to say.
-You can't.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.234
Do you have scenes with him?
-Did he say?

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:41.367
-He said that he's having a lot
of fun with Billy Crudup,

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.934
which --

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:45.000
-Okay.
Well, then I can't say anything.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.300
But -- No, he's the greatest.
-I know. We said that already.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.000
But is he in a scene
with Jennifer Aniston?

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.868
-Uh...
-We don't even know.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.601
We can't say anything.
When is it coming out?

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.067
-Um...
-You can't say that either?

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.267
-I can't say that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.234
All I know is he's amazing.
He's great.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.100
I think it's been everywhere.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.667
He has a whole -- some scenes
with Jennifer Aniston.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:12.334
-Ohh. That's a little hot goss
right there.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.601
-That's a little tea.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:17.300
-I have --
We have something in common.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.767
-We do?
-Yeah.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:23.567
We both love Dolly Parton.
-Well, come on. I can't.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.167
-We have that in common
with a lot of people.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.100
-I mean --
-I was just with Dolly --

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.601
You're going to be jealous.
-What?

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.501
-I shot a --
-Her Christmas special?

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.234
-Yes.
-Didn't get the call.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.534
-Yeah.
-Did not get the call.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.167
-"Mountain Magic Christmas."

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.934
I'm in a full-on scene singing
and dancing with Dolly Parton.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.501
-Stop right now.
-Yeah, it's the greatest.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.868
I went to Tennessee.
-What?!

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.767
-I went to Tennessee --
-And you didn't call me?

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.000
-I didn't ca-- I'm sorry. Yeah.
But you know what I did?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.701
I went to Sevierville,
which is her hometown.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.634
-Yeah.
-And I went to -- I said

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.701
I got to find a local
mom-and-pop barbecue place.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:59.634
So I went and found a place
called Preacher's barbecue.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.267
And I don't know if they watch
the show, but they were awesome.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.868
-They will now.
-And one guy was there.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.801
I went.
It was delicious barbecue.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.434
And I said,
"Do you have T-shirts?

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:08.667
I go, "Do you have T-shirts?

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.200
Cause I'd love to get
just a shirt from you."

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.934
He said, "I could check
in the back, see what we have.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.767
I don't even know
what we have here.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.567
I don't even know
if we have a T-shirt.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.901
People don't buy T-shirts."

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.234
I go, "I don't know."
He goes, "Well, we have one."

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.734
He goes, "It's just a logo."

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.200
And I go, "Yeah.
And what's on the back?"

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.033
And on the back it said,
"We're kind of a pig deal."

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.634
That's the best thing.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:31.701
That's the best thing I could
ever purchase in my entire life.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.100
Now, I know you --
-I need one of those T-shirts.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.701
-Right?
Isn't that a great T-shirt?

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.200
-Yeah.
-I know you've met Dolly

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.868
and talked with Dolly before.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:41.300
-I'm making a movie with Dolly.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.033
Well, I'm -- Okay.
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.868
-Not a Christmas holiday film.
-Well, I mean, sorry.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:48.968
Some of us didn't get invited
on her Christmas special.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.901
But, no, she wrote this book
with James Patterson

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.701
called "Run, Rose, Run."
-That's right.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:56.667
-And my company is producing it.
-You are the greatest.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.033
Come on. Are you kidding me?
You get to work with Dolly?

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.200
-Yes!
-How awesome is that?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.601
-I don't know if she'll let me
be in the movie, but I get to

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.934
stand on the side and go,
"That was amazing."

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.300
-Can we talk about your
production company, by the way?

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.868
Hello Sunshine.
-Aww. Thanks.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:14.067
-Congratulations on --
Everything you're doing...

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.300
-Thank you.
-...turns to gold.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.234
-Thank you.
-It's quality stuff.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.234
It's great stuff.
You just got named by

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.367
"Hollywood Reporter" one of
the TV producers of the year.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.901
-That's so amazing.
-That's a giant deal.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.100
-Yeah.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.767
-Does that mean
more work for you?

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.667
'Cause once you reach that list,
everyone's like,

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:30.901
"Let's just call Hello Sunshine,

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.634
see if she'll produce
something we're doing."

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.367
-Yes, yes, it does, Jimmy.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:37.267
More work is good.
I'm so lucky.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.834
-Isn't it fun to see it grow
and become --

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.167
-It's incredible.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:42.033
And then we get to work
with amazing people.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.367
We have a show with Zoe Saldana
coming out this month.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.300
And then next year we have
a show with Jennifer Garner,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.033
which is really exciting.
-[ Gasps ] Wow!

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.033
-It's just so much cool stuff.

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.300
-Yeah, and the book club
is crushing.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.934
-Yeah, the book club's
doing really well.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You're just -- Everything.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:57.701
I've got to say --
-Doing really well.

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:00.934
-It's because you're a hard
worker and you're just awesome.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.834
This is something I saw

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.901
that you responded to on Twitter
and it made me laugh.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:09.200
It says, "If Reese Witherspoon
and Dwayne the Rock Johnson

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.567
were ever fighting in an arena

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.300
and only one
could come out alive...

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.567
I'd bet my life savings on
Reese Witherspoon winning.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.033
Don't ask me why."

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:19.767
-Wait. Can I tell you a story?

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.701
I actually sent that
to the Rock,

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:24.334
and he's like,
"She's not wrong."

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:26.501
-Wow! Dwayne said it.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.667
-Dwayne's like --
He's like, "Not wrong."

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.334
-Not wrong.

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:31.767
I put my money on Reese
Witherspoon all the time.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.234
-I get a little scrappy, guys.
Don't count out the shorty.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.300
The shorty will come for you.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.534
-Can we talk about "Busy Betty"?
-Yes. Please.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.968
-I love this. My girls
are going to love this.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.067
-Yay!

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:44.367
-I love the illustrations,
by the way.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.367
-Yes. It's all about m--

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.601
I actually, during the pandemic,

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:49.734
I had this idea about a little
girl who builds businesses.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.033
But I was like, "Wait.

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.367
I built a bunch of businesses
when I was little."

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:56.100
So it's all about
how I had a lot of energy.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.167
I was kind of the kid who --
their parents got called to say,

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:02.234
"Reesy's talking a little bit
too much in class today,

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.868
and we're going to have to
separate her from her friends."

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:07.801
But I just had so much energy
and so many ideas.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:10.934
And when my brother
would pitch businesses to me,

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.567
I would be like,
"I could do that."

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.534
And so I started
lemonade stands, magic shows.

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:17.334
And then I started
selling barrettes

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:18.701
out of my desk
in the third grade.

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:20.033
That one got shut down.

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:22.834
-Of course. Famous story.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.133
-Wasn't up to code.
Had supply-chain issues.

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.834
[ Laughter ]
-Supply-chain issues.

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:29.000
-I realized
ever since I was little,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.000
I just loved
building businesses.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.467
-Yeah, and that's good.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.300
I think that's great for anyone
who reads this and goes --

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.033
'Cause when you have a mind
of a child, which...

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.300
-Yeah.
-...some of us do.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.868
-That's what we have in common.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.934
-Yeah. Being creative and just
going, "I've got an idea."

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.767
And you're like, "Oh, yeah.
I want to wash the dog."

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.467
And then it's a disaster,

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.200
but it turns out to be
a great business.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.334
-Yeah, and the good thing
is people like you and me

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:56.300
meet responsible people
who actually keep us on track.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.968
Which are the amazing people
you guys don't see.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.033
They're all standing
behind stage,

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:02.767
but they keep the wheels
on the wagon.

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.701
-Yeah, I wouldn't be here
without everybody.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.234
-Yeah, they're amazing.

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.100
Your team is amazing.
-Absolutely.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:12.234
-Amazing, amazing.
-But I love this because I --

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:14.601
"Busy Betty."
I know who Betty is based on.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:16.033
The name, Betty. It's your mom.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.868
-It's my mom, yeah.
-I love your mom.

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.434
She's so cute.
-I love my mom.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:20.701
And in my dedication, I say,

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.434
"Thank you for encouraging
my magical thinking."

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.767
Because you got to have somebody

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:27.033
who believes in your kookiness,
and my mother did.

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:28.868
-Yeah.
-She just was like --

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.534
She just thought it was great
and funny and charming.

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:33.133
-Yeah. It is good.
And it's a fun book.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:36.300
A funny book. But then
look at the back of the book.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.234
"Busy Betty" is holding a photo.
Look at this cute.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.701
-That's me.

00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:42.634
-That is --
That's the original Busy Betty.

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:44.734
-That's me.
-Wow. Glasses and all.

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:45.968
-Yeah.

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:47.100
-You're already, like,
entertaining.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.501
-Glasses.
-"Hi!"

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:51.300
-My brother's hand-me-downs.
The tube socks with the sandals.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.000
-I love the tube socks.
It's so fantastic.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.167
-The tube socks!
-It is so cute. Come on.

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.734
Congrats on this book and thanks
again for coming on the show

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:00.334
and always playing with us.
We love you.

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:02.734
Reese Witherspoon, everybody.

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:05.200
"Busy Betty" is available now.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.400
Kevin Nealon joins us
after the break.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.300
Stick around, everybody!

